From e2d9ed2ff57e5031e72485d17213fd53cd7a70dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:23:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta Phase 8: full-resolution 3D, touch bindings, save
 import/export, screenshots

* io: IOState::read_overrides serves a host file in place of another for
  read-only opens and stats. ss-delta.exe uses it to hand the game a copy
  of app0:resource/boot_config.ini with changed keys, leaving the
  installed file alone: [display] full_3d (default on) sets ResoDown 0,
  the game's own 960x544 3D mode instead of 720x408; [boot_config] passes
  other keys through (case kept).
* touch: TouchState::held, fingers a frontend holds at fixed points,
  reported with the mouse's. ss-delta.ini [touch] binds keys and gamepad
  buttons or triggers to them; the default holds the Black Rite icon
  (56, 494) on F and the left trigger. Applied for an older ss-delta.ini
  without the section too.
* ctrl input pipe: "touch x y ... | none" and "screenshot <path>".
* renderer: run_on_render_thread, tasks the render thread runs after a
  frame. Screenshots (F12 to ss-delta/screenshots/, and the pipe's) are
  read back there, at render resolution, and written on a thread of
  their own; a read-back from the frontend thread raced the renderer's
  queue submits (VK exception in stop_recording).
* ss-delta.exe --import-save <folder|zip> / --export-save <folder>
  [--quiet]: the save's four files (sizes checked), the previous save
  kept in ss-delta/save-backups/, and Vita3K's slot record written so
  the game's load screen lists the save.
* [debug] frame_rate / frame_rate_delay: the 60 fps study. Sets the
  game's frame timer period and display flip threshold in guest memory.
  Not for play: a quest started at 60 fps never finishes loading.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
